# BusyBox init configuration for zaurus-refresh stage 2.
# Format: <id>:<runlevels>:<action>:<process>

# One-time system setup (mounts, mdev, network, dropbear).
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# Login prompt on the framebuffer console (VT1). getty sets up the tty
# then execs /bin/login. Log in as root/zaurus or piko/piko (change with
# passwd). Respawned if it exits.
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 38400 tty1 linux

# Reboot / shutdown handling.
# ctrlaltdel uses the kexec-based softreboot (not /sbin/reboot's PXA
# watchdog hard reset, which behaves identically to poweroff on this
# hardware -- see usr/sbin/softreboot).
::ctrlaltdel:/usr/sbin/softreboot
# Lazy-detach the SD card FIRST, before the blocking `umount -a -r`.
# If the card was pulled while mounted (or card-detect never fired a
# remove uevent), /mnt/card points at absent mmc hardware; a plain
# umount there flushes synchronously and wedges forever in
# uninterruptible D-state (immune to SIGKILL), so init never reaches the
# final reboot() and poweroff hangs with the kernel still alive (found
# 2026-07-27). `umount -l` (MNT_DETACH) returns immediately -- it defers
# teardown instead of flushing -- so `umount -a -r` afterwards never sees
# /mnt/card and can't block on it.
::shutdown:/bin/umount -l /mnt/card
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::restart:/sbin/init
